        "original_id": "d17803b5-e9ca-59af-af3b-ce8d93796473",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bryan Caplan, Patrick Michaels, Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, Charles Koch\n- Organizations: George Mason University, Mercatus Center, Cato Institute, Freakonomics, EconLog, Greening Earth Society, Western Fuels Association, Koch Industries\n- Roles: economist, professor of economics, research fellow, adjunct scholar, senior fellow, editor\n- Places: Washington, D.C.\n- Topics: libertarian think tanks, environmental studies, newsletters\n\nFacts:\n- Bryan Caplan was born on April 8, 1971, and is an American economist.\n- The Cato Institute was founded as the Charles Koch Foundation in 1974 by Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, and Charles Koch.\n- The Cato Institute is an American libertarian think tank headquartered in Washington, D.C.\n- Bryan Caplan is a professor of economics at George Mason University.\n- Bryan Caplan is a research fellow at the Mercatus Center.\n- Bryan Caplan is an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute.\n- Bryan Caplan is a frequent contributor to Freakonomics and publishes his own blog, EconLog.\n- Patrick Michaels is a senior fellow in environmental studies at the Cato Institute.\n- World Climate Report is a newsletter edited by Patrick Michaels.\n- World Climate Report was produced by the Greening Earth Society, a non-profit organization created by the Western Fuels Association.",
